{"id": "unknown-2026-10-20-009", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Yousee Display offers customizable AMOLED display modules from 1.1\" to 27\", backed by an integrated supply chain", "content": "<p>As demand for customized AMOLED displays grows across smart wearables, automotive systems, industrial equipment and premium consumer electronics, standard display modules often struggle to meet a product's specific design and performance requirements. Shenzhen-based <a href=\"https://www.youseelcd.com/\">Yousee Display&nbsp;</a> addresses this challenge by combining an extensive AMOLED portfolio with deep engineering customization, an integrated supply chain and flexible inventory management - ", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/yousee-display-offers-customizable-amoled-display-modules-11-27-backed", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-10-20-010", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Samsung Display pursues a two-pronged FMM-less strategy, as its MPO lithography process advances alongside inkjet printing", "content": "<p>Samsung Display is pursuing two different paths to replace fine metal mask (FMM) deposition. Just a day after Korea's ETNews <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/samsung-display-build-inkjet-printed-oled-pilot-line-race-replace-fmm\">reported that SDC is in talks with partners to build an inkjet-printed OLED pilot line</a>, THE ELEC reports that Samsung is also progressing with its in-house lithography-based process, Micro Patterned OLED (MPO), and is developing a <strong>7-inch-class FMM-free O", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/samsung-display-pursues-two-pronged-fmm-less-strategy-its-mpo-lithography", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "innolux-2026-10-20-011", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": ["innolux", "auo"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.7, "reasons": ["多公司提及"]}, "title": "AUO selects glass substrate specs for semiconductor processes, not size rivalry", "content": "AUO is tailoring its glass core substrate specifications specifically to semiconductor process requirements rather than competing on panel dimensions with Innolux, according to Chairman and CEO Paul Peng. The company aims to leverage its glass-processing expertise to supply critical components and technologies to outsourced semiconductor assembly and test (OSAT) leaders such as ASE Technology Holding and Powertech Technology.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261020PD237/auo-substrate-lcd-packaging-osat.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-20-012", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Thermaltake expands AI workstation lineup on edge AI demand", "content": "Thermaltake is targeting the growing edge AI market with a new workstation lineup. Chairman Kenny Lin said the company has transformed from a gaming components maker into an AI PC and workstation systems provider. The company plans to launch three product lines in the second half of 2026 and aims for AI-related products to contribute 5% to 10% of revenue in 2027.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261020PD232/thermaltake-workstation-gaming-market-revenue.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-10-20-013", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["[否定]expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Samsung's HBM4 supply lock-in exposes limits of China's CXMT as Apple and Tesla seek DRAM alternatives", "content": "Samsung Electronics is expected to enter 2027 with approximately 80% of its planned memory production secured under long-term contracts, reinforcing its pricing position while China's ChangXin Memory Technologies (CXMT) expands capacity and attracts attention from US tech companies seeking alternative DRAM suppliers.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261020VL218/samsung-cxmt-dram-hbm4.html", "type": "rss"}]}
