{"id": "lg_display-2026-10-20-020", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_display", "lg_elec", "boe"], "customers": ["lg_elec"], "suppliers": ["lg_display", "boe"]}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "HKC evaluates large-area WOLED line for TVs and monitors panel production", "content": "<p>According to UBI Research, China's <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/hkc\">HKC</a> is evaluating an investment in a third OLED project, called H8, following its H6 and H7 projects. While the first two projects target small, medium and IT displays, H8 will reportedly be a large-area OLED line for TVs and monitors - and HKC's internal assessment favors white OLED (WOLED) technology. If this project goes ahead, HKC will become the world's third WOLED producer, after LG Display and BOE.</p><p><a ", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/hkc-evaluates-third-oled-project-likely-large-area-woled-line-tvs-and-monitors", "type": "rss"}]}
